# inc-bsqm reproduction: read the over-cap miss in Creature::GainInherentBonus.
#
# The run LOADS the frozen orc barbarian (INCURSION_LOAD, set by
# tools/check_inh_wasteful.sh; fixture orc-barbarian-seed1-opt0818), so no
# character generation runs. The barbarian's creation already granted STR and
# CON inherent bonuses; DEX has none, so the probe's arm starts from a clean
# attribute. The script takes a +5 "Treatise of Efficious Celerity" (the DEX
# tome, lib/m_items.irh:58) from wizard Item Acquisition and reads it from the
# pack. That read is the run's FIRST GainInherentBonus call: with
# INCURSION_INH_PROBE=1 the probe (src/Creature.cpp) arms A_DEX just before it
# and writes the result to logs/inh.log.
#
# @choose needs the "(in pack) " prefix FindMenuEntry draws (src/Wposix.cpp
# MenuLabel/NameMatches match from the start of the line).
w
y

@choose "Item Acquisition"
@until "]: Tomes" RIGHT
@until "Treatise of Efficious Celerity" DOWN
@expect "Treatise of Efficious Celerity"
DOWN
ENTER
"5" ENTER
@while "Air'" s
@while "ESC:Done" ESC
r
@choose "(in pack) Treatise of Efficious Celerity"
@while "--More--" ENTER
@while "ESC:Done" ESC

@dump:probed
@quit
